WEBVTT

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.750
December 31st, New Year's Eve.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.500
The Okayama City Shopping District
was packed with shoppers

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.660
looking for New Year's items
and good luck charms.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:27.080
Everyone was getting ready to welcome in the new year.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.790
"Black beans"
Everyone was getting ready to welcome in the new year.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.410
"Happy New Year"

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.040
Oh, no! I forgot!

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.750
Maina? What did you forget?

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.500
Don't worry.
There's still time before the concert.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.830
Reo, I-I...

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.950
Yup, yup.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.080
I forgot to buy some New Year's black beans!

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.450
Yup... Hm?

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.540
What should I do? I can't properly
ring in the new year without them.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.370
I'm sure you'll be able to buy them
after the concert. Don't worry.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.540
You're right. Actually, the ones
left over might even be half price.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.660
It's already New Year's...
This year sure flew by fast.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.750
But so much happened.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.330
Like Girls' Festa and the sports festival...
And of course, the popularity ranking.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.120
Thank goodness Reo
didn't break her leg this year.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.700
How long are you going to keep bringing that up?

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.830
I'm not happy with how
this year turned out at all.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.040
I'm going to be in the Girls' Festa next year,

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.000
and there'll be a total A-ya storm
that takes over

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.040
the sports festival and ranking next year!

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.000
You're so amazing, Aya.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.160
I mean, she's got no way to back this up.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.830
But that was the most Aya thing she could say.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:44.870
That's even more reason to do our best
at our final concert of the year

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.950
and ring in the new year.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.250
So that we can all go to the Budokan.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.700
The Budokan.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.500
I personally don't really care
about going to the Budokan.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.660
Want some?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.000
"Happy New Year"

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.540
This is the first time I get to spend
the end of the year with my fave.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.370
This is the first time I get to spend
the end of the year with my fave.
"Not as a Wota, But as a Person"

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.120
There's some mysterious excitement I'm feeling--

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.200
Kumasa! Eripiyo's just up and died in here!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.040
It'd be a shame if the concert was canceled,
so please come back to life soon.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.540
Repairs?

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.870
Apparently, that lightning that fell
on Christmas applied the final blow.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.370
Wait. If they're not going
to be performing here, then Cham...

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.660
Correct. There are no performances
here for a month.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.620
And since they don't have a venue,

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.330
that also means no Maina
birthday celebration in January.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:22.290
Just how unlucky can she be?

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.330
"Unlucky"
Maina's so unlucky she's cute!

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.620
Why are you so excited?

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:31.080
Well, Eripiyo is the type of person who looks at

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.120
the pictures on Maina's blog and goes,
"It's sunny in the background. How cute!"

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.790
Maina's so cute!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.500
The rest of the world has taken the hint

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.450
and bestowed Maina with the unlucky attribute!

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.580
Yumeri's birthday celebration will be a day late,

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:48.370
but thank goodness it just barely survived.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:52.500
The world must be blessing Yumeri
along with the end of the year.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.540
God damn you, world!

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.330
If you're not going to bless Maina,
then you can just be destroyed!

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.120
I don't even know what to say.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.660
Regardless, I'm not sure if
Eripiyo would've been able to

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.120
pull off a proper birthday celebration.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.750
How rude!

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.370
"The Celebrate Maina's Birthday Party"
Maina's birthday should be
celebrated throughout Japan,

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.370
"The Celebrate Maina's Birthday Party"
therefore, I declare that I
will make it a national holiday!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.330
Are you just going to skip
the Okayama government

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.410
and go straight for the national government?

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:21.580
Guys! You had nothing better to do
on New Year's Eve, either?

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.410
Yeah!

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.790
Yuka, seriously, stop that.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.870
Everyone's really busy,
but making time to come see us.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:34.580
Let's have fun until the very last
moment of this year!

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.910
Yeah!

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.450
Thank you for everything this year!

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.790
Have a wonderful new year.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.450
Don't choke on any mochi and die!

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.160
It was a wonderful year.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:58.250
Thank you for all your support!

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.620
Just know that I know all
the faces of the people

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.660
who supported me and those who didn't!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.540
Th-Thank you very much.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.410
We hope you'll continue supporting us next year.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.000
Thank you from all of us, too!

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.700
What a great way to end the year.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.410
It's over...

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:26.370
The level of despair I'm feeling right now
is enough to engulf the whole world in darkness!

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:33.000
Could you not ruin everyone's happiness
with such cursed words?

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Today's the last show of the year,
so we're having a special merch booth

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.700
to show our thanks!

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:39.830
Special merch booth?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.250
--This is the first time we're trying it,
so we're nervous, too.
--What?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.290
--This is the first time we're trying it,
so we're nervous, too.
--I'm so curious.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.450
--Nice.
--I wonder what I should have her say.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:52.870
What am I going to do? We can have them
record anything we want them to say?

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:56.790
This can only be classified as a godly
event planned by a divine management.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:00.540
Now, Eripiyo will be able to return
to this world after falling into darkness--

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.290
Eripiyo, I wuv, wuv, love you so much!

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.000
This world is filled with hypocrisy,
but Eripiyo's existence

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.700
is the light that shows me the way
down the path to become a top idol.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.080
But I get lonely sometimes, because I'm a girl!

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.450
When that happens, I'll just imagine Eripiyo's smile
within my heart as I lay down to sleep,

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:10.410
hoping we'll be reunited in my dreams!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:13.330
Yes! This should be doable in five seconds.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.290
You can't make the five seconds
from your dimension

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:18.000
the same as Maina's five seconds.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.410
No problem!

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.830
Time means nothing when it comes to words.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.950
You're insane, you know that?

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:28.540
And that was the least likely thing
that Maina would say.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.160
"Special merch booth"
We will now begin the special merch booth.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.700
What would you like me to say, Kumasa?

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:40.410
Um... Then how about,
"Kumasa, it's morning. Wake up"?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:41.580
Okay!

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:46.540
Kumasa, it's morning. Wake up!

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:49.120
I hope you listen to my voice every day.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.120
Thanks!

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.580
What would you like for your message?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:57.120
Hm... I'm not sure.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.910
"Motoi, I love you!"

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.620
"Motoi, we're having instant curry tonight."

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.620
"Darling, I love you!"

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.750
No! I can't choose just one!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.950
Motoi, don't cheat on me!

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.540
Wait! Did you actually record that?!

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.410
I won't cheat on you...

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.500
I know.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:15.500
Squee...

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Huh?

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.200
Um... Eripiyo...

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.450
--Wait!
--Huh?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:42.950
Could you make it out to Eri? I need you to
address me not as a <i>wota</i>, but as a person!

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.450
What?!

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:47.790
As a person? As another woman?!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.000
No one asked you to go that far.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.450
As for the message, "Eri, support me!"

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.870
I'll listen to it when I get sick of work.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.870
Eri, support me!

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.330
--This is the best.
--Eri, support me! Eri, support me!

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:04.200
--The vibration caused by Maina's voice...
--Eri, support me! Eri, support me!

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.700
--It feels like Maina's inside my body...
--Eri, support me! Eri, support me!

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:08.830
Um...

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:12.040
Eripiyo's talking about internal organs again.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.580
Wait... Was that too creepy?!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.330
Um... I...

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:23.330
I need to come up with something good to say
when she mentions internal organs again...

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.540
Gah! She's creeped out!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.620
F-F-F-Forget what I said!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.120
--Huh?
--Have a Happy New Year!

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.540
Well, have a great New Year, you two.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:35.790
Reo's going to be on a countdown show,
so I'm going to the studio to watch.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:39.660
Lucky... I want to ring in
the new year with Maina, too!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.410
If I don't hurry up and go home,
I'm probably going to have to ring in

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.080
the new year with you, so bye!

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.040
Really?

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.200
Okay, see you in a month.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.700
Yeah, see you in a month.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.790
A month usually goes by super fast,

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.160
but thinking about not being able
to see her makes it feel really long.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:06.290
I won't be able to see her for a month,
and I made our last encounter super awkward!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.160
I'm home.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.370
Welcome home. Now, help me with New Year's food.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:16.370
Sure...

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.290
For the love of...

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:25.290
I'm a pro when it comes to flipping over bread.
I'm also a pro at supporting people.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.870
Then just stand there and support me.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:30.540
There's just something I've gotta say!

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.120
Sakiko's the cutest, just so you know!

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:37.040
What're you doing, Eri?

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.790
Did you start working yet, Eri?

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:42.660
I-I currently flip over bread...

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.080
I meant a real job, not a part-time one.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.660
Wait, Eri. You still don't have a job?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.370
Er, I think I still have some time to decide...

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:55.080
Keep saying that and you'll be
an old maid before you know it.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.120
There's someone I want to introduce you to, Eri.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.370
He's a great guy. He's so amazing that

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:03.620
he's had five different wives.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:05.750
U-Uh...

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.040
If you don't get a job now, when will you?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.700
There's nothing more important
than finding a career.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:15.500
Listen, make sure you appreciate
that they're letting you work for them.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:19.000
You can't wait for Mr. Right forever, Eri.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.750
Eri, let's play some games.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.000
I don't hear you cheering for me, Eri.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:35.250
This is why I hate spending
New Year's at my house...

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.450
There are only 30 minutes left this year!

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:43.950
On this program, we look back on
the past year with celebrities from Okayama.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.370
Here are our guests for today!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:51.200
The comedians from Okayama,
Chieko Bloomers with V!

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.450
Hello!

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:56.750
Mr. Otomo from Ibara, who is a <i>shigin </i>poet
and won the Demi Katsudon Award.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.450
Thanks for having me!

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:01.790
"Reo Igarashi"
And we also have Reo Igarashi, who's an idol in Okayama.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.700
Good evening!

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:08.700
This is the first time I'm on a show
like this on my own, so I'm a bit nervous.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:12.370
Looks like a lot of your fans
showed up in support.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.080
Thank you, everyone.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.250
So, you're usually performing
with a group, right?

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:23.200
Yes. The rest of the members
of ChamJam are all minors,

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:27.250
so I'm a bit sad they weren't
able to join me today.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.750
"Lightly sweetened"
"Special Selection Black Beans"
"Half price"

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:34.870
But I think they're all watching right now.

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.500
We are!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.000
No fair! No fair!

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:45.160
Must be nice being able to ring in
the new year with your fave!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.660
Damn it! How can I sit here
and eat soba at a time like this?!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.540
"Motoi, let's go to our first
shrine visit of the year right now!"

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.540
Send!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.040
"Welcome"
"Saijo Inari Shrine Entrance"

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:07.120
Hey!

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.790
Eripiyo, Happy New Year.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.450
Happy New Year!

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:15.160
I'm glad you're the first person I'm seeing
other than family this year, Rena!

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.950
Hey, I'm here, too.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.500
That's pretty rude after you called me
out here in the middle of the night.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:22.000
"Welcome"
"Saijo Inari Shrine Entrance"

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:25.620
Just thinking about the fact that Sorane

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.330
might be ringing in
the new year with a boyfriend...

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:29.620
I couldn't sleep at all.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.450
But you know those rumors aren't true.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.540
Yeah, but...

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.660
At the same time,

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:40.450
we only know the version of them
we see at concerts and events.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.080
Yeah...

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:46.790
And after we spend so much of the year
just thinking about our faves...

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:52.700
I wonder if Maina thinks
about someone like this, too.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.080
Maina-<i>chin</i>!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:02.250
Yuka. Happy New Year.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.580
HNY!

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:07.450
You trying not to get recognized? You idol, you.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.950
I'm just trying to not catch a cold.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:15.870
Not to mention... There's only one person
who'd actually recognize me.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.580
Huh. Well, let's go.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:19.580
Sure.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.580
It's a bit sad that we won't have
another concert for a month.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.080
But now we can do a short-term part-time job.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.040
A part-time job, huh...

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.450
They just all keep bugging me
about finding a real job.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.200
You're so lucky, Rena.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:40.160
You probably don't hear stuff like that
since you're in high school.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.080
But I have entrance exams this year,

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:44.410
so I won't be able to go
to any concerts for a while.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:48.700
Really? I'm sure Maina
would love to see you, too.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.910
But they're off until February, so...

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.660
Yeah...

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.160
But...

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.750
Is something wrong?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.750
I had a really weird encounter with her yesterday,
so things are super awkward!

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:04.540
I don't want to have to deal
with this awkwardness for a month!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.450
I can't wait until the next concert.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.910
But things are so awkward!

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:10.660
What in the world did you do?

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.450
I'm sure it'll be okay.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.620
I'm pretty sure Maina's not worried about it.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.000
Rena!

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:19.250
Oh, my gosh! You're the nicest little sister!
How about I buy you an <i>ema </i>plaque?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.410
Just a reminder that she's my little sister.

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:24.370
Or rather, we're just fans.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:25.580
What?

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:30.830
I don't think the idols really
worry about us too much.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.910
I need you to address me
not as a <i>wota</i>, but as a person!

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:38.160
I really done messed up!

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:46.450
We're finally here.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.250
Guess I'll pray.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:51.040
Here's a whole <i>gacha </i>pull amount! There!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:05.370
I hope that ChamJam will be able
to go to the Budokan.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:06.370
Also...

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:11.750
...I hope Eripiyo doesn't get hurt anymore.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.660
Please let Maina be healthy all year again.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:33.790
Please let Maina eat yummy things every day.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.370
Please let Maina be happy.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:39.290
Please let Maina go to the Budokan.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.620
Hey, did you wish that I get into college?

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:46.910
You probably only made a wish for yourself.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:50.250
I ended up wishing for my own
good health. Sorry.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.330
Honestly...

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:55.870
Well, I guess I only made
a wish for myself, too.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:59.080
I totally forgot to make a wish for myself!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.750
Huh? Then who did you make a wish for?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:02.700
Oh.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.000
Oh...

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.540
Wait, what? Why do you two seem so distant?

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:11.580
Wait! I don't really care about Motoi,
but don't leave me, Rena!

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:14.080
You seem way colder towards me lately.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.790
Rena!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.290
This <i>amazake </i>is so good!

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.750
It sure warms you up.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:24.290
What did you wish for?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.160
Did you wish for the Budokan, too, Maina-<i>chin</i>?

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.410
I did. Wait, did you also wish
for the Budokan, Yuka?

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:30.410
Yup!

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:34.700
But you said you didn't really care
about going to the Budokan.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.160
I did. That's because as long
as I get to be an idol,

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.910
I don't care where I perform.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:45.120
It's so fun having a total stranger
tell me how much they love me.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.700
I don't care where I perform,

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:50.750
as long as more people tell me
how much they love me.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:55.080
But at yesterday's concert...

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.330
Heya! What did you want me to say?

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.790
I'll say whatever you want me to!

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:04.660
Then, could you say,
"We're going to the Budokan" for me?

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.700
Huh? That's all you want?

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.450
It is.

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:13.200
I want you to say,
"I'll see you at the Budokan, Fumi."

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:16.580
Really? You want me to mention the Budokan, too?
Why, though?

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:19.830
You don't seem that interested,

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:24.660
but we want to see you singing
and dancing at the Budokan.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.870
If everyone who loves me is saying that,

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.660
I guess I don't mind going to the Budokan.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:34.500
Sorry, I totally thought you
wished for something else.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:35.540
You know, something like,

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.540
"I hope I get to eat a bunch of
non-conveyor-belt sushi," or something.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:41.870
Wait, what?
That's a really lame diss, Maina-<i>chin</i>.

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:46.160
While we're at it, I wanna be
the center at Budokan!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:51.250
Did you know? You have to have
odd numbers to have a center.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.250
I do.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.250
So there needs to be seven of us.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:55.250
Yeah.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:57.250
Huh?

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:02.910
Hey! Maki-<i>chin</i>! Yume-<i>chin</i>!

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.290
Y-Yuka?!

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.160
Hey, keep it down!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:09.660
Don't worry. We're not so famous
that we'd actually cause a ruckus.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:11.870
That's not the problem here.

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.200
Happy New Year!

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:14.830
H-Happy New Year.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:17.830
You guys sure are close,
spending New Year's together.

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:21.410
Um, well, you know. We didn't want
to get separated in the crowd...

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.660
I mean, I wasn't asking about that, but sure.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:24.620
See?

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:26.950
Oh, right.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.950
We made it!

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.250
We didn't get separated, thanks to this!

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:42.000
It's good that you brought it.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.450
I wonder how long until the first sunrise.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:49.410
Fear not! Morning always comes!

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.950
And Cham is going to shine brighter than ever!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.700
There you go, randomly
proclaiming epic things again.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:01.250
Speaking of ringing in the new year,
did you watch Reo on the countdown show?

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.000
I did. But...

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:08.950
Five, four, three, two, one...

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:12.450
"Happy New Year"
Happy New Year!

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:14.910
Kumasa kept catching my attention so much

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:17.200
that I didn't even pay
attention to the countdown.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.950
He was super creepy, right?!

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.660
I realized that's how I probably look
to others and decided to reflect a little.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.660
But...

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.450
He looked so happy.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:29.790
Yeah.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.040
I thought it was great.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.370
Hey, did you guys watch Reo's show?

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:38.080
--Yeah.
--I did!

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:39.540
"Happy New Year"

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:43.250
Reo-<i>chin </i>was looking right at her fans
when the new year started.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.450
I thought that was great.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.790
She got to ring in the new year with her fans.

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:48.750
Yeah.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.000
I'd love to do that someday, too.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.830
Oh, fine. I guess you could
just stare at me instead.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:55.950
Why, though?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:11.000
I might just be another fan to Maina,

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:16.410
but she's the one who showed me how
happy I could be giving my all to one person.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:21.750
If Maina made it to the Budokan, I could die.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:24.950
If Maina made it to the Budokan, I could die!

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:28.660
Actually, if Maina did make it
to the Budokan, I would die!

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.370
She actually said that three times...

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:37.450
Maina! I'll love you again this year!

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.000
Huh?

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:46.250
What's up, Maina-<i>chin</i>?

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:48.330
Huh? Oh, nothing.

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:53.040
I thought I just heard Eripiyo's voice,
but it couldn't be...

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.950
Well, we saw the first sunrise
of the year, so let's go home.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:58.000
Wait, we're going home already?

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.000
I think I'm getting a bit tired, too, Yuka.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.700
You guys are no fun!

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:05.370
Aya-<i>chin</i>'s got her part-time job in the morning.

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:07.250
Reo-<i>chin</i>'s at home sleeping.

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:09.620
And Sorane-<i>chin </i>is at some relative's house!

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:13.830
The next time Cham gets together
isn't until February!

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:16.620
I'm sure we'll be doing something
outside sometime in January.

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:20.250
Our management is pretty late
at announcing things.

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:22.160
Guess you're right.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:25.370
Then I'll be able to see Eripiyo, too.

00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:28.290
Then I guess our outside performance
in January will be at the Budokan!

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:30.330
Yeah, probably not...

00:24:05.660 --> 00:24:07.750
Your countdown show was amazing, Reo!

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.910
I totally saw you look at me first
as soon as the new year started.

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:13.370
But I didn't get invited
to the first shrine visit...

00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:15.580
R-Reo? Are you going to cheer me up?

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:18.160
Thank you! Okay, I'm starting to feel better!

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:19.950
"Your Fave Isn't Your Friend"
--Thank you very much!
--Kuma, Kuma, Kuma...
